Product Vision & Project Overview

Version: v1.0

Status: Draft

Author: Tejas Nere

1. Introduction

PrepFlow is a modern learning platform designed to help Class 11, Class 12, and MHT CET students prepare in a structured, organized, and distraction-free way.

Instead of spending hours searching for YouTube videos, notes, formula sheets, and previous year questions across multiple platforms, students will find everything in one organized place.

PrepFlow focuses on reducing confusion, saving time, and making learning structured through chapter-wise learning paths and progress tracking.

The platform is not another coaching website or content platform. It is a preparation operating system that organizes existing learning resources into a clean, trackable, and student-friendly experience.

2. Problem Statement

Students preparing for MHT CET often depend on free resources available on YouTube and other platforms.

Although high-quality resources exist, students face several challenges during preparation.

Common problems include:

Incomplete YouTube playlists
Different teachers following different teaching sequences
Resources scattered across multiple platforms
Difficulty finding trusted study material
No proper chapter-wise organization
No centralized progress tracking
Time wasted searching instead of studying
Difficulty revising completed chapters
Lack of structured learning roadmap

Students often spend more time searching than actually studying.

3. Proposed Solution

PrepFlow solves these problems by providing a centralized platform where students can access carefully organized learning resources chapter-wise.

Each chapter contains all required learning resources including playlists, notes, formula sheets, previous year questions, and other study material.

Students can track their progress resource-by-resource, chapter-by-chapter, subject-by-subject, and overall.

The platform removes decision fatigue by always guiding students towards the next step in their preparation journey.

4. Vision

To build the most organized and student-friendly preparation platform that helps students study efficiently without wasting time searching for resources.

5. Mission

To simplify the preparation journey by organizing quality learning resources into a structured roadmap that saves time, improves consistency, and increases productivity.

6. Target Users

Primary Users

Class 11 Students
Class 12 Students
MHT CET Aspirants

Future Expansion

JEE Aspirants
NEET Aspirants
Competitive Exam Students
School Students
7. Core Philosophy

Student Philosophy

Do not make students search.

Make them study.

Admin Philosophy

Do not make administrators write code.

Make them manage content.

Platform Philosophy

Every click should reduce confusion.

Every screen should help students understand what to study next.

8. Primary Goals

The primary goals of PrepFlow are:

Organize study resources chapter-wise
Save students' preparation time
Reduce decision fatigue
Improve learning consistency
Track learning progress
Provide a structured preparation roadmap
Create a clean and distraction-free study experience
9. Product Principles

PrepFlow follows these principles throughout development.

Principle 1

Students should know what to study within three seconds of opening the platform.

Principle 2

Everything should be organized.

Principle 3

Everything should be trackable.

Principle 4

Everything should be simple.

Principle 5

Learning should never feel confusing.

10. Platform Identity

PrepFlow is not:

A coaching platform
A YouTube alternative
A note-sharing website
A learning management system

PrepFlow is:

A structured preparation platform
A study operating system
A learning roadmap
A centralized resource management platform for students
11. Long-Term Vision

The first version of PrepFlow focuses on structured learning and resource organization.

Future versions will include:

AI-powered study planner
Battle Mode
Live Leaderboards
Revision Planner
Mock Tests
Community Features
AI Learning Assistant
Personalized Recommendations
12. Success Criteria

PrepFlow will be considered successful when students:

Spend less time searching for resources
Study more consistently
Complete chapters in an organized manner
Track their progress easily
Return to the platform daily
13. Project Motto

Stop Searching. Start Studying.

14. Closing Statement

PrepFlow is designed with one simple objective:

Help students spend less time searching and more time learning.

Every feature, every screen, every interaction, and every future update will follow this philosophy.

The platform aims to become a complete preparation operating system where students can organize, track, and complete their learning journey efficiently.